<h1>The relay's build list</h1>
<p class="muted">
  Every fact the Manager asked for and nothing could answer, read out of
  <code><%= Cove.wants_file %></code>. This page is the API specification for the relay, and it is
  written by need rather than by design: a want whose count stops climbing is a function the relay
  has grown.
</p>

<h2>Asked for, not answered</h2>
<% if @wants.empty? %>
  <div class="note">nothing wants yet — open a <a href="<%= pods_path %>">pod page</a> and the Manager will ask.</div>
<% else %>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>want</th><th>agent</th><th>times</th><th>first</th><th>last</th><th>last reason</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <% @wants.each do |w| %>
        <tr>
          <td><code><%= w["want"] %></code></td>
          <td><%= w["agent"] %></td>
          <td><%= w["count"] %></td>
          <td class="muted"><%= w["first_seen"] %></td>
          <td class="muted"><%= w["last_seen"] %></td>
          <td class="muted"><%= w["reason"] %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
<% end %>

<h2>What each want means</h2>
<table>
  <tbody>
    <% @declared.each do |key, meaning| %>
      <tr><td><code><%= key %></code></td><td><%= meaning %></td></tr>
    <% end %>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>How the Manager asks</h2>
<pre>GET <%= @relay_template %>%{agent}/facts?want=&lt;want&gt;

200 {"value": &lt;measurement&gt;, "detail": &lt;optional string&gt;}
with anything else  ->  {"seen": false, "reason": "&lt;why&gt;"}

The wire carries measurements. Verdicts, if any, belong on the Manager's side of it.</pre>
<p class="muted">
  Template from <code>COVE_RELAY_URL_TEMPLATE</code>; address per agent is
  <code>%{agent}</code> substituted with the sheet's slug. If the relay's real address turns out to be
  different, the first thing that will say so is a page full of refusals whose reasons all name the
  same wrong address.
</p>
